  "wait_modes": {
    "native": "Runtime native wait: DG2 short spin then WDDM OS event; Intel UMD fence wait in control.",
    "poll": "Same bounded pause loop: Runtime::ready() versus Commands::ready()."
  },
  "caveats": [
    "Both data heaps are resident CPU-visible system memory; allocations are separate.",
    "ISA placement, cache policy, state programming and native wait implementation differ.",
    "Native wait uses an OS event on WDDM and the driver's fence wait on L0.",
    "Poll uses pause loops with bounded completion checks on both backends.",
    "These workloads use no scratch/private memory; new scratch/private GPU execution remains unvalidated.",
    "Dispatch completion latency is not full-model token throughput.",
    "Polling occupies a CPU thread; GPU clocks are not fixed.",
    "ISA and captured arguments live in separate allocations in the reusable backend."
  ],
